<speak>That is a useful way to organise future contact. A brief agenda can set expectations without turning the meeting into a formal presentation. We can keep it to the broad purpose and any practical preparation, rather than a long list that makes the appointment seem more complicated than it is. For the digital session, the device can simply be charged and available. For a general meeting, your own questions can be the starting point. I will also avoid combining unrelated administrative reminders in the invitation itself, because that would undo the clarity you are asking for. Each message should have a recognisable purpose.</speak>